// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0
// Donor: rustc FnCtxt -- taken (one explicit receiver per check run, holding
// the state its walk rides on, beside Go's *Checker and Roslyn's Binder).
// Role: the Checker RECEIVER type -- the state of one check run, cut from
// check.nv 2026-09-29 (decision 12, the file-size cap): check.nv keeps the
// shape walk, this peer keeps the state the walk rides on. One module, one
// namespace -- the type is visible to every peer exactly as before.
// Used by: the whole check module; nothing outside imports it.
// Guarded by: check-novac-file-size.py (this file exists because check.nv
// crossed the cap).
// novac/src/check/checker_type.nv

module novac.check

/// State of one check run: the source (for positions), the semantic context
/// and the diagnostics collected so far. A receiver, not a triple of
/// parameters on every function — the shape of every reference (Go
/// `*Checker`, Roslyn `Binder`, rustc `FnCtxt`, Zig `*Sema`).
///
/// WHY NOT AN EFFECT (owner's question, 2026-08-16). Nova's effects model
/// CAPABILITIES and control — `Fs`, `Os`, `Fail`, `Supervisor`; the
/// compilation context is pure data. An ambient context (a) hides the data
/// flow, and the §3/§4 map rests on that flow being visible ("what flows
/// along the edge" is guarded), (b) pays a TLS-vtable cost on every read
/// in the hot `type_of` loop, under П14 "speed is priority #1", (c)
/// diverges from the references: rustc keeps `TyCtxt` explicit, and the
/// ambient `ty::tls` is left only for diagnostics and debugging.
type Checker {
    src SourceText /// the file text: the one source of positions
    ctx Ctx /// type registry and callable table, read from the declarations
    /// THE name index over ctx.fns (274.4 step 2): built here, held here, and
    /// nowhere else -- emit_c and mono get a Ctx and no index, so resolution
    /// after the checker is not merely forbidden, there is nothing to call.
    res FnIndex
    /// THE name index over ctx.fields (274.4 step 3): the same lock for the
    /// field root -- fields resolve only through a receiver type, and only
    /// the checker can ask.
    fres FieldIndex
    /// The FIRST gap seen in this file — a refusal whose run has zero width,
    /// that is, a token the grammar required and nobody wrote. Held rather
    /// than said at once: a gap points at nothing the author typed, so it is
    /// the LAST thing worth saying about a file, and only when nothing with
    /// width was said. `gap_at < 0` means none seen.
    gap_at int
    /// WHAT was wanted at `gap_at`, when the door that planted the gap knew.
    /// `TokenKind.ErrorTok` means it did not: gaps planted by recovery carry no
    /// expectation, and the refusal then says only that the text is not a form
    /// of the language -- the message this field exists to improve on (#850).
    gap_kind TokenKind
    out []Diagnostic /// diagnostics collected by this run
    chan CheckOut /// THE channel this run publishes: what the checker decided (sem.CheckOut)
    scope Scope /// locals of the function body being typed; reset per function
    /// One-entry table reused by the self-initializer check (274.3/F28). It is
    /// a FIELD and not a local because the lookup door must not build anything
    /// (P18/P14): a table allocated per binding turns an O(1) question into an
    /// allocation on the hot path of every `ro`/`mut` in the file.
    self_probe NameTable
    /// Top-level names already seen in THIS file (#811). sem cannot report --
    /// it holds no diagnostics -- and it silently keeps the FIRST declaration
    /// of a repeated name, so the second one has to be refused here or not at
    /// all. One table per run, the same shape `self_probe` is.
    seen_decls NameTable
    /// The instance's substitution: `substs[i]` is the concrete type standing
    /// in type-parameter slot `i`. EMPTY for an ordinary run over a file, and
    /// that emptiness is what tells `type_fn` to skip a generic body -- there
    /// is nothing to type it under. One copy of the body is typed per
    /// instance (Go stenciling), so nothing here is parametric afterwards.
    substs []TyId
    /// The ONE block whose tail call is a returned value: the body of the fn
    /// being walked, when that fn declares a return type (274.5 wave B4). Set
    /// by the FnDecl arm of each phase, read by the Block arm; there are no
    /// nested fns, so one slot is the whole state.
    tail_value_body NodeId
    /// THE RETURN THE BODY BEING TYPED MUST PRODUCE (274.7 B5, registry #960):
    /// the declared return type of the fn under `type_fn`, concrete for an
    /// instance, `no_ty()` when there is nothing to judge -- no declaration, a
    /// unit return, or a type parameter (an instance judges its own body;
    /// "I do not judge" is the answer for the generic shape). Read by the
    /// return door at every tail and every `return`. One slot, like
    /// `tail_value_body`, for the same reason: there are no nested fns.
    ret_expect TyId
    /// The type the value being typed RIGHT NOW is expected to have, or
    /// `no_ty()`: set by the return door around a tail or `return` operand
    /// (to `ret_expect`), cleared by a call around its arguments. Read by the
    /// one form the language types from its context alone -- a bare variant of
    /// a GENERIC sum (`None`, wave W4), whose instance is not in the token.
    value_expect TyId
    /// Loops around the node being walked (274.7 B10): `break`/`continue` at 0 are refused.
    loop_depth int
    /// The body being typed returns no value (`-> ()` or none declared): a bare `return` is legal.
    ret_unit bool
}
